         3,
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "On \\( [2, 3] \\), \\( f(x) - g(x) = - 3 x^{2} + 15 x - 17 \\), which is positive, so f is the upper curve and the limits are the given vertical lines.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99059",
         "rule_named": "upper minus lower"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{2}^{3} \\left(- 3 x^{2} + 15 x - 17\\right)\\,dx \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "area between curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the integrand is \\( - x^{3} + \\frac{15 x^{2}}{2} - 17 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "power rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluating from \\( 2 \\) to \\( 3 \\), the area is \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            2
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
